{"availability":"available","full":"FluxoGen/ease","name":"ease","description":"Ease — a symptom-first self-acupressure PWA (React + Vite + TypeScript). Wellness education only.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T06:23:55Z","updated":"2026-10-10T10:33:30Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://ease-murex.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://ease-murex.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T05:05:19.114Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T05:05:19.114Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T05:05:19.114Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.140Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T05:05:19.114Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ease is an offline-capable PWA for self-acupressure: pressing points on your own body for everyday symptoms (not needle acupuncture). It is symptom-first. Pick what is going on, get a short routine of points, each with a drawing, a plain-language way to find it, and a guided timer.","Wellness education only. Not medical advice. Language is \"traditionally used for\", never \"treats\"."],"features":["Search-first home: symptoms, body parts, point names/codes and everyday phrases (\"can't sleep\").","Body map (/map): tap where it hurts (front/back) to see that area's symptoms and points.","All points (/points): search plus area and channel filters over the whole library.","Point page: picture, \"Find it\", technique, cautions, evidence chip, and a guided press","(full-screen timer, 4 s in / 6 s out breathing dot, side switching, screen wake lock, next-point hand-off)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FluxoGen/ease/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"59856e9e1aa55253914e0739a930c7a32409b02a3fd00cd93abc0bf0a8778517","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.218Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:43.218Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ease is an offline-capable PWA fo